======================================================================
SYNTHESIS
======================================================================

THE RESONANCE DECOMPOSITION:
  μ(LONELY) = OUTSIDE_CREDIT + PAIRWISE_DEBT + HIGHER_DEBT

  OUTSIDE = ((n-2)/n)^{n-1} ≈ e^{-2} ≈ 13.5% for large n
  PAIRWISE = negative (cancels part of outside)
  HIGHER = the remaining correction

  For INITIAL SEGMENT: OUTSIDE + PAIRWISE + HIGHER = 0 exactly
    (wall-only lonely, measure 0)
  For OTHER speed sets: OUTSIDE + PAIRWISE + HIGHER > 0
    (positive lonely measure)

  The PROOF TARGET: show |PAIRWISE + HIGHER| < OUTSIDE
  for all non-initial primitive speed sets.
  Equivalently: the initial segment MAXIMIZES the debt.

  This is the RESONANCE DEBT CONJECTURE:
  Among all primitive speed sets at a given n, the initial segment
  {1,...,n-1} has the maximum |debt/credit| ratio, equal to exactly 1.
  All other speed sets have ratio < 1, proving LRC.

